# A block named by the former spelling `var` is no data of a launch (the author 2026-11-11: the special name is
# `data`): in the code of Code its head `var` is an ordinary name, which the launch does not find -- answer 3 at the
# call. Named `data`, the same block is the data child the code skips, and the launch gives 2 (the fixture code_data).
Code:
    var:
        int: x 1
    end: var
    x := x + 1
end: Code
call: Code\var Code
int: seen Code\var\x
